---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import EventsList from "@dst/ui/EventsList.astro";
import { forum, forumDate, otherEvents } from "../content";
---
<Layout
  title="Dubai future-tech events"
  description="A calendar of the Dubai conferences on the subjects Future World Forum covers — smart cities, PropTech, digital finance and mobility — with dates, venues and what each one actually is."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Calendar</p>
    <h1>Dubai future-tech events</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Future World Forum is one date in a crowded season. These are the other
      Dubai events on the same subjects, with the detail the listings tend to
      bury: who runs it, where it actually is, and what kind of room you would
      be walking into.
    </p>
    <p>
      Looking for the forum itself?
      <a href="/" title="Future World Forum Dubai 2026 — dates, tickets and programme">Future World Forum Dubai 2026</a>,
      {forumDate}, is on the front page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <EventsList items={otherEvents} />
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Why these and not others</h2>
    <p>
      Every entry here has a named organiser, a confirmed venue and a source
      that can be checked — the same bar this site holds
      {forum.title} to, and the reason its own venue line still reads
      "not announced". Dubai's calendar has dozens of technology events; the
      ones listed are those whose subjects overlap the forum's five sectors
      and whose details are actually published.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
